# Code owners (https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners).
# A pull request touching these paths asks the owner for review; with "Require review from
# Code Owners" in the branch protection of main (docs/dev/RELEASE.md, "Branch protection") it
# cannot merge without it.  CONTRIBUTING.md explains why each area is protected.
# Later lines take precedence over earlier ones for the same path.

# the bit-exact ports of the original and their frozen output (parity and bit-exact rules)
/mlaser/parity_ports/   @rahilm
/tests/golden/          @rahilm
/tools/make_goldens.py  @rahilm
# the C emitter kernel (bit-identical to the Python port), the NC compiler and the card protocol:
# they decide the bytes on the wire
/mlaser/_native/        @rahilm
/mlaser/nc/             @rahilm
/mlaser/protocol/       @rahilm

# machine safety: the card supervisor, streamer, interlocks, the safety state machine,
# pre-flight and lifecycle, and their tests and documentation
/mlaser/controller/     @rahilm
/mlaser/machine/        @rahilm
/tests/safety/          @rahilm
/docs/SAFETY.md         @rahilm

# the guards themselves
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @rahilm
/.github/workflows/parity-guard.yml @rahilm
/tools/parity_guard.py              @rahilm
/SECURITY.md                        @rahilm
